Executor Service :
- Executor service is an interface which we used to create and manage a pool of threads.
- Executor service is most common interface which is used to manage the thread pool in executor framework.

public class Main{
    public static void main(String [] args){
        ExecutorService executorService = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(3);    //Number of threads wants to create inside pool.
    }
}


# Methods in executor service
execute() method takes runnable as parameter and its return type is void();

submit() methods takes runnable as paramter and it returns a future interface.
        (Both are overloaded methods)
submit() method takes callable as paramter and it returns a future interface.

executorService.shutdown() it stops the running process at the end.



